    "body": "Here is what `shellcheck` thinks about it:\r\n```\r\nLine 439:\r\n      eval \"`starship init tcsh`\"\r\n            ^-- SC2046: Quote this to prevent word splitting.\r\n            ^-- SC2006: Use $(...) notation instead of legacy backticked `...`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nFirst of all AFAIK, you don't need to quote _backticked_ portion so it can be simplified to:\r\n```tcsh\r\neval `starship init tcsh`\r\n```\r\n\r\nand to incorporate that nicely into the existing script use the following form:\r\n```\r\n  ${BOLD}${UNDERLINE}Tcsh${NO_COLOR}\r\n  Add the following to the end of ${BOLD}~/.tcshrc${NO_COLOR}:\r\n\r\n      eval \\`starship init tcsh\\`\r\n```\r\n\r\nEscaping backticks prevents SC2006 false positive.",
